```{r, include = FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(
  collapse = TRUE,
  comment = "#>"
)
```

Confidence intervals for
R-squared,
semipartial correlations,
squared partial correlations,
the improvement in R-squared,
and Cohen's f-squared
are generated using
the `RSqDelta()`, `SCorDelta()`, `PCorDelta()`, `DeltaRSqDelta()`,
and `FSqDelta()` functions from the `betaDelta` package.
In this example,
we use the data set and the model used in
[betaDelta: Example Using the BetaDelta Function](example-beta-delta.html).

```{r}
#| message = FALSE
library(package = "betaDelta")
```

```{r}
#| echo = FALSE
if (!exists(x = "nas1982")) {
  try(
    expr = utils::data(
      "nas1982",
      package = "betaDelta"
    ),
    silent = TRUE
  )
}
df <- nas1982
```

```{r}
#| eval = FALSE
df <- betaDelta::nas1982
```

## Fit the regression model using the `lm()` function.

```{r}
object <- stats::lm(formula = QUALITY ~ NARTIC + PCTGRT + PCTSUPP, data = df)
```

## Estimate the standardized regression slopes and the sampling covariance matrix.

```{r}
std_mvn <- BetaDelta(object = object, type = "mvn")
std_adf <- BetaDelta(object = object, type = "adf")
```

## R-squared and adjusted R-squared

```{r}
summary(object = RSqDelta(object = std_adf, alpha = 0.05))
```

## Semipartial correlations

```{r}
summary(object = SCorDelta(object = std_adf, alpha = 0.05))
```

## Squared signed-semipartial correlations

The interval of the signed semipartial correlation, squared as a set.

```{r}
SCorSqDelta(object = std_adf, level = 0.95)
```

## Squared partial correlations

```{r}
summary(object = PCorDelta(object = std_adf, alpha = 0.05))
```

## Improvement in R-squared

```{r}
summary(object = DeltaRSqDelta(object = std_adf, alpha = 0.05))
```

## Cohen's f-squared and local f-squared

```{r}
summary(object = FSqDelta(object = std_adf, alpha = 0.05))
```

## Comparing covariance estimators

```{r}
stats::confint(object = DeltaRSqDelta(object = std_mvn), level = 0.95)
stats::confint(object = DeltaRSqDelta(object = std_adf), level = 0.95)
```

## Extracting estimates, sampling covariance matrices, and confidence intervals

The `coef()`, `vcov()`, and `confint()` methods
work on the output of every effect-size function.

```{r}
scor <- SCorDelta(object = std_adf)
stats::coef(object = scor)
stats::vcov(object = scor)
stats::confint(object = scor, level = 0.95)
```

